{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-aa3b4385-05a5-44b8-a46d-eba038c451ab","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9043e14c56fe6a8a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-3c6rm759/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Run linkage on registered model versions\n\n## Description\n\nRegistered model versions in the Model Registry record a resolvable link back to the run (training or pipeline run) that produced them, and that linkage is exposed through the registry's existing entity and REST API surfaces so platform consumers — including the Dashboard's registry experience — can resolve a model version to its originating run. This epic delivers the registry side of the model-version-to-run linkage; the Dashboard-side entry point that consumes it is a separate epic owned by the Dashboard team.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Support recording the originating run on a registered model version using the registry's documented model-version metadata extension point (custom properties on ModelVersion entities) or an equivalent supported mechanism — the specific mechanism is an implementation decision for the Model Registry team.\n- Expose the run linkage through the registry's OpenAPI-specified REST API so consumers can read the originating run for a given model version.\n- Ensure model versions registered from runs in the platform carry the linkage (population at registration time, whether via registration flows or client SDK usage).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered from a run in the platform, When the version is read via the registry REST API, Then the originating run is resolvable from the version's metadata.\n- Given a model version with no known originating run, When read via the API, Then the linkage is absent or empty without errors (backward compatible with existing model versions).\n- The linkage mechanism is documented in the registry's API surface (OpenAPI) so downstream consumers can build against it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1, registry side)**: \"Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them\" — the data/API half of this requirement is covered by this epic; the \"so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry\" (UI) half is covered by the Dashboard registry-experience epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34928,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcbd6419c04ac19d","agent_id":"a013fad8e4f4b1efe","session_id":"f3b104a1-b56c-4bb7-a36a-1ff96392a602","uuid":"21402b3a-ded2-4d0b-af25-6806c2f620b3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:09:01.280Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
