ocs describe the comparison workflow, which must exist first. |\n39\t| E002 → E004 | 11 | Docs cover the registry-side linkage; must exist first. |\n40\t| E003 → E004 | 11 | HLR-4 explicitly covers the workflow \"from both the runs list and the registry\". |\n41\t| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | 14 (different repos, no shared artifacts) | odh-dashboard vs model-registry — fully parallel start; the P0 comparison work is not gated by the P1 registry linkage. |\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n44\t\n45\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n46\t|-----|----------|---------|\n47\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 |\n48\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 (registry data/API side), E003 (Dashboard registry UI side) — split by component/team boundary (Epic Boundary Rule 1) |\n49\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (bundled with HLR-1) — the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run data (same component, same team, same data structure); the strategy itself notes wording overlap consolidated from two customer councils. Splitting would build the same surface twice and add an artificial serialization edge, so both HLRs are covered by one epic at the higher priority (P0). |\n50\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 |\n51\t\n52\tFull coverage: HLR-1 through HLR-4 all map to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n53\t\n54\t## Health Warnings\n55\t\n56\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list with no change descriptions or owner teams. Teams were therefore taken from the architecture context files (`dashboard.md` → RHOAI Dashboard, `model-registry.md` → Model Registry, `data-science-pipelines.md` → RHOAI Pipelines). Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs in lieu of strategy ACs.\n57\t- **Passive component classification**: Data Science Pipelines is listed as affected but the strategy describes no change to it. The