{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b628ea5d26da765","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Run linkage on registered model versions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run linkage on registered model versions\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRegistered model versions in the Model Registry record a resolvable link back to the run (training or pipeline run) that produced them, and that linkage is exposed through the registry's existing entity and REST API surfaces so platform consumers — including the Dashboard's registry experience — can resolve a model version to its originating run. This epic delivers the registry side of the model-version-to-run linkage; the Dashboard-side entry point that consumes it is a separate epic owned by the Dashboard team.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Support recording the originating run on a registered model version using the registry's documented model-version metadata extension point (custom properties on ModelVersion entities) or an equivalent supported mechanism — the specific mechanism is an implementation decision for the Model Registry team.\n38\t- Expose the run linkage through the registry's OpenAPI-specified REST API so consumers can read the originating run for a given model version.\n39\t- Ensure model versions registered from runs in the platform carry the linkage (population at registration time, whether via registration flows or client SDK usage).\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- Given a model version registered from a run in the platform, When the version is read via the registry REST API, Then the originating run is resolvable from the version's metadata.\n44\t- Given a model version with no known originating run, When read via the API, Then the linkage is absent or empty without errors (backward compatible with existing model versions).\n45\t- The linkage mechanism is documented in the registry's API surface (OpenAPI) so downstream consumers can build against it.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- **HLR-2 (P1, registry side)**: \"Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them\" — the data/API half of this requirement is covered by this epic; the \"so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry\" (UI) half is covered by the Dashboard registry-experience epic.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b0b2a8f6cf7032e","agent_id":"a7bbe4cbb23cf47a6","session_id":"f3b104a1-b56c-4bb7-a36a-1ff96392a602","uuid":"25cdd1b6-58df-4bc0-a647-567ad38f82ce","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:11:05.971Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b628ea5d26da765","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
