{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8859fa24dc796c9d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E003\n3\ttitle: Open run comparisons from the Model Registry\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 7\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Open run comparisons from the Model Registry\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tIn the Dashboard's registry experience, a registered model version surfaces the run that produced it, and the user can open a run comparison from there. This epic consumes two capabilities delivered elsewhere in the strategy: the run-comparison surface in the Dashboard (side-by-side and diff views over selected runs) and the run-linkage data recorded on registered model versions by the Model Registry. It depends on both — the entry point opens the comparison surface and reads the version's run linkage.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- In the registry UI (model version view), surface the originating run recorded on the model version.\n40\t- Provide an action to open the run comparison for the linked run, landing in the run-comparison capability with the linked run selected so further runs can be added for side-by-side or diff comparison.\n41\t- Keep the registry-originated comparison consistent with the runs-list-originated comparison (same surface, same data rendering).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given a registered model version with a recorded originating run, When the user views the version in the registry UI, Then the originating run is shown and an action to open its comparison is available.\n46\t- Given the user invokes that action, When the comparison opens, Then it is populated with the linked run and ready for side-by-side and diff comparison against other runs.\n47\t- Given a model version with no recorded originating run, When viewed in the registry UI, Then the version renders normally with the comparison action absent or disabled (no errors).\n48\t- The registry-originated comparison renders parameters and metrics identically to the runs-list-originated comparison.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- **HLR-2 (P1, UI side)**: \"so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry\" — the user-facing half of the requirement, covered by this epic on top of the registry-side run linkage.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b0b2a8f6cf7032e","agent_id":"a7bbe4cbb23cf47a6","session_id":"f3b104a1-b56c-4bb7-a36a-1ff96392a602","uuid":"4b3a598d-9dc3-4eeb-b695-e774bec36973","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:11:06.671Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8859fa24dc796c9d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
